  "notes": "Scholarly article published in Revue d’assyriologie 93 (2001), pages 39–66. It reconstructs House F at Nippur from local archaeological and tablet-typological evidence. The title’s phrase ‘A Scribal School’ identifies the article’s scholarly interpretation. ISAC 2023 and Robson’s 2026 return to House F provide later controls on locality, temporality, community, formation, and interpretation. Current coverage is bibliographic, with source-reported authorship awaiting review.",
